				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-13964573/scp-5365</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Tue, 29 Dec 2020 18:15:20 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Pedagon</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>5903100</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>How do you write about an infectious disease in a global pandemic? Apparently you just have to make it cute!</p> <p>I had a lot of fun writing this SCiP for <span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=2826105&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1609270035" alt="Rigen" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=2826105)" /></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/rigen" >Rigen</a></span> for the holiday exchange! When I first got the prompt of making “art or tale about anomalous disease SCP/SCPs&quot; I was really unsure of what to do since I couldn't figure out a way to do a tale about a disease without paralleling the current pandemic (and I honestly didn't realize that the request was for art or tale rather than an SCP until like 2 days before the due date). But I think what came out is fun and people have said it’s funny, cute, and really clever so I guess others agree! Happy Holidays everyone!</p> <p>Writing Critters: Orgath, Dr. Whitney, Grigori Karpin, HarryBlank, Dysadron, Dr. Chandra, RadioactiveRADs, Radguel, Phiiota, Ralliston,</p> <p>Science Critters: Opal and Solari</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
